From 122bb99184e7ff3438e436c501d44ec727575869 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:00:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 192/225] feat: dynamic meshes in the software triangle ray
 tracer (stage 3A)

Movable brushes, entity meshes and characters near the camera now appear in
ray traced reflections. One global BVH over them is rebuilt every frame into
the DYN_MESH segment (records 0..30719) with its materials in DYN_MATS, root =
record 0 - the shape Neo's captures show. The consumer needs nothing new: the
shader already walks the dynamic root every ray.

- Collection (CSvoEnv::Render, main thread, every frame - the tree walk below
  it is time throttled): eERType_MovableBrush / _Brush / _Character within
  e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistCam * e_svoTI_RT_DynObjDistRatio, filtered to exactly what
  CheckCollectObjectsForVoxelization leaves out of the static soup: characters
  always, brushes whose GI mode is not eGM_StaticVoxelization, and brushes
  flagged ERF_MOVES_EVERY_FRAME (their soup copy is stale by construction).
  eGM_HideIfGiIsActive and eGM_IntegrateIntoTerrain are honoured, proxies and
  hidden nodes dropped, objects sorted by projected size under the budget.
- Geometry: IRenderMesh CPU streams (LockForThreadAccess, GetPosPtr/GetUVPtr/
  GetTangentPtr, index stream, per chunk sub material) at the LOD chosen by
  e_svoTI_RT_LodRatio, plus compound CGF sub objects and character attachments.
  Skinned meshes use their bind pose placed by the character's world matrix -
  CE 5.7.1 skins on the GPU and the CPU fallback writes into a write only
  vertex buffer, so no CPU skinned positions exist; bone mounted stat objects
  do follow the animation.
- Build: per object BVH built once with the static SAH builder in object local
  space and cached by (render mesh, lod); a rigid move is a refit - node boxes
  recomputed bottom up from the transformed triangles, triangles requantised
  against the object's world bounds. A per frame median split top level over
  the object bounds is flattened into the same tree; object depth + top level
  depth stay within the consumer's 18 level stack, and objects past the top
  level cap merge into one leaf instead of a deeper node.
- Upload: the whole dynamic region is rewritten each frame, the tail that the
  previous frame used is zeroed so a stale subtree can never be walked, and
  CheckUpdateMeshPools() now runs before the trace of the same frame.
- e_svoTI_RT_SelfTest gains a dynamic case: two cached objects under a top
  level, a second frame with one moved, a third with one dropped (tail zeroing)
  and a fourth with 70 objects that exercises the overflow leaf - 4 x 1000 rays
  against brute force, 0 mismatches, 0 stack overflows, 0 stale texels.
- New cvars (the renderer mirrors none of them): e_svoTI_RT_Dynamic,
  e_svoTI_RT_DynObjDistRatio, e_svoTI_RT_DynMaxTris, e_svoTI_RT_LodRatio.
  New HUD line "RT dyn: ...". Everything stays behind e_svoTI_RT_Active.

